{"name":"Blank Canvas","hex":"#ffefd6","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blank canvas","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An unmarked or empty state, offering a limitless potential for creation, development or interpretation.","Used other than figuratively or idiomatically: see blank,‎ canvas."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blank_canvas"}],"entries":[{"title":"Blank Canvas (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Blank Canvas is a 2009 documentary film about the creation of 'We Unfold', a contemporary dance work. The film was directed by Tim Slade and features Spanish-born choreographer Rafael Bonachela and the Sydney Dance Company."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blank_Canvas_(film)"},{"title":"The Music","blocks":[{"text":"The Music were an English alternative rock band, formed in Kippax, Leeds in 1999. Comprising Robert Harvey, Adam Nutter, Stuart Coleman (bass) and Phil Jordan (drums), the band came to prominence with the release of their self-titled debut album in 2002. The band released two further studio albums, Welcome to the North (2004) and Strength in Numbers (2008), before parting ways in 2011."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Music"},{"title":"Canvas","blocks":[{"text":"Canvas is a durable plain-woven fabric used for making sails, tents, marquees, backpacks, shelters, as a support for oil painting and for other items for which sturdiness is required, as well as in such fashion objects as handbags, electronic device cases, and shoes. It is popularly used by artists as a painting surface, typically stretched across a wooden frame."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Sj%C3%B6manss%C3%A4ck_-_1991.jpg/330px-Sj%C3%B6manss%C3%A4ck_-_1991.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canvas"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/MetroBrussel_Erasmus.jpg/500px-MetroB